      "text": "The root cause is that `Statevector.from_label` takes a single bitstring and builds a basis state, not a phase oracle. Passing it a list fails, and even a single label would not flip the phase of the target states, which is what Grover's oracle needs. The fix builds a diagonal phase oracle that multiplies the amplitudes of `|101⟩` and `|110⟩` by -1, and passes that circuit to `GroverOperator`.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Statevector\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit.circuit.library import GroverOperator, Diagonal\n\ntargets = ['101', '110']\n\n# FIX: Statevector.from_label cannot take a list and builds a basis state rather than a phase oracle -> build a 3-qubit circuit with a Diagonal gate that sets phase -1 on each target index, because GroverOperator needs a phase-oracle circuit\ndiag = [1] * 8\nfor t in targets:\n    diag[int(t, 2)] = -1\noracle = QuantumCircuit(3)\noracle.append(Diagonal(diag), [0, 1, 2])\n\ngrover_op = GroverOperator(oracle)\nprint(grover_op)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
